**Issue**: #425
**Date**: 2026-09-24
**Status**: Approved
**Author**: NMG
**Related Spec**: specs/409-reconcile-independently-merged-failed-deliver-checkpoint/

Feature: Release a stopped controller only after independently proven terminal delivery
  A stopped issue must never be replayed or silently discarded.

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Archived #206 evidence permits the next explicit issue
    Given the retained cancelled implement checkpoint, owner ledger and strict handoff for PennyScan #206
    And PR #208 uniquely closes #206 at its recorded head on the default branch
    And the checkpoint head is an ancestor of PR #208's exact head and its merge is on the clean default checkout
    And no worker or foreign controller owns the old run
    When a distinct approved issue is explicitly selected
    Then the original evidence and owner records are archived byte-exact with digests and a receipt
    And only the active run pointer is released before the new issue starts through ordinary dispatch
    And #206 is not replayed or represented as a new successful worker run

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Changed or ambiguous delivery evidence blocks
    Given the retained stopped checkpoint
    But its issue is open, PR is unmerged, head or branch differs, closing PRs conflict, base differs, or ancestry is absent
    When a different issue is explicitly selected
    Then the exact missing proof is reported and no worker starts
    And the checkpoint, handoffs and recovery ledger are unchanged

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Unsafe local evidence blocks release
    Given a symlinked, missing, partial, changed or colliding evidence archive
    Or a dirty or non-default checkout, active worker, foreign controller lease, ambiguous recovery owner or conflicting session delivery
    When a different issue is explicitly selected
    Then the original active checkpoint and supporting evidence remain unchanged
    And no old or new issue worker starts

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: Repeated admission cannot repeat reconciliation
    Given the prior run was archived and its pointer released before a new run started
    When the next issue is invoked again
    Then the original receipt and archive remain immutable
    And no duplicate archive or old recovery consumption occurs

  @SCN005 @regression @readonly
  Scenario: Current #217 failed delivery safely admits #218 without live mutation
    Given immutable byte-and-hash snapshots of PennyScan #217's failed-deliver run and all strict handoffs
    And PR #230 uniquely closes #217 at its exact head on the default branch
    And the checkpoint is an ancestor of that PR head while the merge is on the clean default checkout
    When isolated explicit #218 admission uses those snapshots and stubbed GitHub and Herdr responses
    Then the #217 run, handoffs, owner ledger, standalone sessions and referenced recovery archive are preserved with a digest receipt
    And only the isolated active pointer is released before the ordinary #218 worker starts
    And the live PennyScan #217 runtime remains unchanged and undispatched
